 <field name="NAME">
  <value>Lesson 1. Basics of circuit design</value>
 </field>
 <field name="PREVIEW_PICTURE">
  <value name="archive_video_1.webp" type="file">iblock/c65/8npxw3aqqbmw3n1c3ciiuzhs1ojstolq.webp</value>
 </field>
 <field name="PREVIEW_TEXT">
  <value>The video discusses the concept of electric current, its main parameters: voltage, resistance, current; the relationship of these parameters through Ohm's law. Then the main elements that can be found in an electrical circuit are analyzed: resistors, capacitors, diodes, LEDs, connectors, microcircuits. It shows how to read electrical circuits and what the electrical circuit and the device board have in common. At the end of the video, the main points of working with a laboratory power supply and a multimeter are shown.</value>
 </field>
